ana (devex): Heads-up — onboarding reported a Typescript quickstart that uses old CommonJS require() and the legacy method name createCompletion. New SDK uses ESM imports and generate(). New users hit a runtime error when following the guide.

ana (devex): Snippet from README: ```ts
// OLD - CommonJS + legacy API
const Redwood = require('redwood-sdk');
const client = new Redwood.Client(process.env.REDWOOD_KEY);
const res = await client.createCompletion({ prompt: 'hi' });
console.log(res.text);
```

jules (docs): Oof. That will blow up in modern TS projects (and with "type": "module"). We should show both ESM + an explicit tsconfig snippet for beginners.

prateek (sdk): I'll draft a replacement that uses ESM and the correct method: ```ts
// GOOD - ESM + typed imports + async usage
import { RedwoodClient } from 'redwood-sdk';
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
const resp = await client.generate({ input: 'hi' });
console.log(resp.output);
```

prateek (sdk): Also will add a short note about npm v7+ defaulting to ESM in projects with "type":"module" and recommend pinning minimal tsconfig for the quickstart.

jules (docs): Please update the quickstart page and the code sample referenced by the onboarding checklist. The existing CI link-check flagged a broken example.

ci-bot: docs-test: failure -> quickstart/typescript/README.md: runtime mismatch detected; example uses deprecated API name. See job #2021

ana (devex): Can we add a docs-lint rule to detect CommonJS require() in TS files or deprecated method names like createCompletion? Those keep resurfacing in copy/paste.

prateek (sdk): Good idea — I'll add a small rule to our docs-validator to scan fenced ts/tsx blocks for "require(" and for deprecated API tokens. Adding a unit test to the SDK repo so future renames fail CI.

jules (docs): I'll also add an inline migration note in the changelog so early adopters know to upgrade code patterns.

ana (devex): Thanks! Small fix but saves a bunch of "why does my build fail" posts. If anyone spots other language quickstarts with old API names, drop them here. :sparkles:
